Step 8: Implement Cart, Checkout and Order Confirmation

Core prompt: Build a complete purchase flow, from adding items to a cart, through checkout, to a final order confirmation screen. All state should be managed client-side with no real payment processing required.

Key features:
1. Cart
  - Add items to cart from any product listing or detail page
  - Support quantity adjustment (increment / decrement / manual input) per line item
  - Remove individual items; show empty state when cart is cleared
  - Cart icon in navbar shows live item count badge
  - Cart persists across page refreshes via localStorage
  - Cart accessible as a slide-over drawer or dedicated /cart page (pick one and stay consistent)

2. Checkout Flow

  - Multi-step or single-page form with clearly separated sections:

    - Contact — name, email, phone
    - Shipping — address line 1 & 2, city, state/province, ZIP, country
    - Payment — card number, expiry, CVV, cardholder name (mock only — no real processing)

  - Client-side validation on every field before advancing
  - Order summary panel visible throughout checkout (items, subtotal, tax, shipping cost, total)
  - "Back" navigation between steps without losing filled data
  - Disable submit button while processing (show loading state)

3. Order Confirmation page (/order-confirmation)
  - Shown immediately after successful mock checkout
  - Display: unique order number (randomly generated), itemized list, shipping address, estimated delivery date, total charged
  - Clear CTA to continue shopping (back to home or product feed)
  - Prevent revisiting confirmation via back button after session ends (or show a graceful "order already placed" state)

Technical requirements:
  - Cart state managed via context / store — not prop-drilled
  - cartService or equivalent utility handles all add / remove / update / clear operations
  - Payment fields must never be stored in state beyond form submission
  - Tax and shipping calculated as simple flat/percentage mock values (define constants, don't hardcode inline)
  - All forms keyboard-accessible; submit on Enter where appropriate
  - Loading and error states on the checkout submit action